# @cover src/lib/common/text_advanced.spl 80%
"""
## Purpose and audience
Contract for the text helper library (`src/lib/common/text_advanced.spl`):
P1 case conversions (to_kebab_case, to_pascal_case, to_screaming_snake),
character transforms (chars_map, tr, gsub), tokenization (split_n, cut,
contains_any), and the P2 predicates, character ops, search, replacement,
radix parsing, and quote helpers. Audience: engineers changing the text
helpers and callers relying on their exact outputs.

## Operator workflow
Run this file with the Simple test runner from the repository root
(`simple run test/unit/lib/std/common/text_helpers_spec.spl`). Scenarios
call the real helpers and pin the transformed output, index, or predicate
verdict against named expected values.

## Compatibility and limitations
The search-result family (index_of, find, find_str, rfind, last_index_of)
returns a raw i64 and uses -1 for not-found, never nil — coalescing their
results is dead on the not-found path and corrupts a genuine index 3. One
predicate scenario uses an explicit lambda to sidestep the filed placeholder-
lambda parser defect noted inline. Edge inputs (empty strings, empty char
sets) are pinned per helper.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A failure names the helper and the input that changed behavior; re-run the
single scenario and compare against the expected value in the assertion
before changing the helper. The -1-vs-nil sentinel scenarios are the ones
that never worked historically — treat any regression there as a runtime
encoding change, not a test artifact.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/lib/strings/strings.md ;
# doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/interpreter_shared_text.md ;
# doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md
# @manual_section: text helpers
# @cover src/lib/common/text_advanced.spl 80%

use std.spipe.*
use std.text_advanced.*

